# app/frontend/public/static is a committed symlink to /var/www/static/ — an
# absolute path that only resolves inside a container with the shared_volume
# mounted. Vite copies public/ wholesale when building, so in a clean image it
# stats a dangling link and the build dies with ENOENT. It exists purely so the
# dev server can reach Django's collected static; the SPA never references
# /static/, and in production WhiteNoise serves it from the backend.
app/frontend/public/static
